cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hermeneutic, please cite it as below."
title: "hermeneutic: an evidence-first drift gate that mines AI chat-log corrections to gate the next response"
abstract: >-
  hermeneutic is an evidence-first drift gate that catches AI response drift
  before it ships by mining chat logs for the corrections a user already made,
  classifying the drift, and running those patterns as a three-stage pre-flight
  gate on outgoing drafts (zero-LLM regex, optional hermes-rubric scoring, then a
  bring-your-own-calibration LLM critic, PressureProbe). It targets silent failure
  modes that aggregate evals and observability miss.
type: software
